# Copy to ~/.bernstein.conf and edit. Every setting is optional and can also be given as a flag
# on the command line where one exists, which wins. This file is read, never run: KEY=value lines,
# # comments, optional quotes, and a leading ~ in a path means your home folder. Only what belongs
# to this machine goes here; nothing secret.

# The lobster-project template new-lobster copies from (kept outside this repository).
#TEMPLATE=~/projects/code/bernstein-code/templates/lobster
# Where new non-code projects and new code projects go.
#NON_CODE_DIR=~/projects/non-code
#CODE_DIR=~/projects/code
# The model and effort every session of a new project is asked to confirm first.
#MODEL=opus
#EFFORT=high
# lobster-mail, and the mail root it uses.
#LOBSTER_MAIL=~/projects/code/lobster-tools-code/lobster-tools/lobster-mail
#MAIL_ROOT=~/projects/mail
# The Python that makes each tools project's .venv.
#PYTHON=/usr/bin/python3
